From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:20:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] test/images/resource-consumer: consume-cpu measures itself on
 FreeBSD

consume-cpu throttles itself by its own CPU use, read through the
systemstat package, which only has stubs outside Linux (zero samples).
On FreeBSD it saw no CPU use and spun: asked for 250m it used about
600m, so the HPA tests saw wrong load and didn't scale as expected.
Measure user+system time with getrusage(2), as the Windows version does
with GetProcessTimes (250m -> 2.0 s of CPU in 8 s, 500m -> 4.0 s).
---
